Abstract

AI

The paper explores the intersection of technology and statistical education, emphasizing that technological advancements should not fundamentally change established educational principles. It highlights the need for innovative strategies in teaching statistics and underscores the importance of empirical research to understand how technology influences statistical learning. The authors assert that better collaboration among researchers, educators, and technologists is crucial for developing effective teaching practices and addressing existing challenges in statistical education.

